WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:02.018 --> 00:00:04.369
<i>[Referee's Whistle Blows]</i>

2
00:00:04.438 --> 00:00:06.938
Let's have a nice.
clean game. everyone.

3
00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:11.193
<i>Put 'em down.</i>

4
00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.325
<i>[Booth] Move the puck.
Wendell. Move it! Move the puck.</i>

5
00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:18.116
<i>- [Player] Up here. Booth. Up here!
- [Player #2] Go!</i>

6
00:00:18.185 --> 00:00:20.668
<i>[Player] Back on "D"!</i>

7
00:00:20.737 --> 00:00:23.221
<i>Pick 'em up on "D." Pick 'em up!</i>

8
00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:28.109
<i>[Brennan] Go. Booth!</i>

9
00:00:28.178 --> 00:00:30.963
Wooh! Go. Booth! Come on!

10
00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:35.284
Kill 'em. Booth!

11
00:00:35.352 --> 00:00:37.669
[Brennan] Whoa! Wow.

12
00:00:37.738 --> 00:00:41.707
What'd he do that for? It's what Booth
does... keeps the other team honest.

13
00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:44.754
He's what you call an "enforcer."
Oh. like law enforcement?

14
00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:48.098
Yeah. okay. Well.
let's go with that.

15
00:00:48.732 --> 00:00:50.415
<i>[Booth] Whoa! What was that?</i>

16
00:00:50.484 --> 00:00:53.001
What about the cross-check?
Ref. are you blind?

17
00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:57.039
<i>Carlson. I'm open.
Pass it! I'm open!</i>

18
00:00:57.107 --> 00:00:59.352
- Pick him off!
- [Number 25] Yes!
- <i>[Whistle Blows]</i>

19
00:00:59.376 --> 00:01:01.909
<i>That was a cheap shot. Carlson.</i>

20
00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:04.496
- [Carlson] Yeah. you guys su...
- <i>[Whistle Blows]</i>

21
00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:07.716
- That's 24 blue.
two minutes for charging.
- <i>[Booth] For what?</i>

22
00:01:07.785 --> 00:01:09.963
- What about
the cross-check back there?
- Get in the box!

23
00:01:09.987 --> 00:01:11.581
Come on. man. It's hockey.

24
00:01:11.605 --> 00:01:14.273
Club hockey. Some of us still
have to go to work in the morning.

25
00:01:14.341 --> 00:01:16.903
[Referee] Enough. Let's go. <i>[Player]
Carlson. calm down. Skate away.</i>

26
00:01:16.927 --> 00:01:18.360
<i>[Carlson] Just
go over in the box.</i>

27
00:01:18.429 --> 00:01:20.924
Get in there and sit down. Let's
go. <i>Yeah. Sit down. crybaby.</i>

28
00:01:20.948 --> 00:01:23.498
- Uh-oh. - [Referee] Let's go.

29
00:01:23.566 --> 00:01:28.370
<i>So. this is punitive. right... to
be sent to this little area here?</i>

30
00:01:28.438 --> 00:01:32.374
Keep your head up next time.
Number 12. Keep your head up!

31
00:01:32.442 --> 00:01:35.910
<i>[Carlson] Yeah. yeah.
I'll be waiting.</i> Come on!

32
00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:38.730
- Hi.
- It's called the penalty box... you know. "sin bin."

33
00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:43.284
<i>Yeah. Booth committed a penalty when he checked
the big guy when he didn't have the puck.</i>

34
00:01:43.353 --> 00:01:45.771
<i>[Number 25] Stay with
him. Carlson. Stay with him!</i>

35
00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:48.390
<i>There's a hit right there.
ref. that you missed. Again!</i>

36
00:01:48.459 --> 00:01:52.777
Booth seems quite anxious to
get out of the disciplinary box.

37
00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:55.147
Yeah. I've never seen
him this agitated before.

38
00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.575
Open man! Open man!

39
00:02:00.387 --> 00:02:02.887
[Cheering]

40
00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.906
That's not good. right? No.

41
00:02:06.477 --> 00:02:09.093
Go. Booth! Wooh-wooh!

42
00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:11.179
[Referee] All
right. Let's go here.

43
00:02:14.017 --> 00:02:16.034
Ooh. Wendell might get a basket.

44
00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:22.074
<i>[Booth] Elbow. ref! Elbow!</i>

45
00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.592
Ooh. is Wendell okay?
That can't be legal.

46
00:02:24.661 --> 00:02:27.479
- It definitely is not.
- [Blows Whistle]

47
00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:30.081
<i>[Player] Come on.
ref. You gotta call that.</i>

48
00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.283
Come on. What are
you doin'. Carlson?

49
00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:35.515
Wanna go? Come on. Come on.

50
00:02:35.539 --> 00:02:38.239
Let's go. Come on. Let's go!

51
00:02:38.308 --> 00:02:41.075
- <i>[Players Chattering]</i>
- [Brennan] Whoa.
- <i>[Player] Come on. Booth!</i>

52
00:02:41.144 --> 00:02:43.678
You're a dirty player.
Carlson! [Grunts]

53
00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:46.664
<i>- Come on. ref. Stop the fight.
- Get your hands free!</i>

54
00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:49.184
<i>- Get your hands free!
- Come on. Carlson. You got him!</i>

55
00:02:49.253 --> 00:02:50.652
<i>Hit him!</i>

56
00:02:50.721 --> 00:02:52.954
Don't take shots at
my guys. You got that?

57
00:02:53.023 --> 00:02:55.624
It ends here. okay. Carlson?

58
00:02:55.693 --> 00:02:57.876
- Oh!
- Ooh!

59
00:02:57.928 --> 00:03:00.595
- Oh!
- [Grunts]
- Ends here!

60
00:03:00.664 --> 00:03:03.710
- Booth seems to be winning.
- Well. it's not Booth
I'm worried about.

61
00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:05.895
<i>This guy's out of
control! Come on. ref!</i>

62
00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:09.972
Hey. hey! I'm gonna have to call
a game misconduct on that one.

63
00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.218
Get up off the ice. we'll
finish this in the parkin' lot.

64
00:03:12.242 --> 00:03:15.060
<i>If you did your job. I
wouldn't have to do it for you.</i>

65
00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:17.406
Go on. Look at him.
He's hittin' my guys!

66
00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:21.450
- <i>[Player] You all right. buddy?</i>
- [Booth] Son of a bitch.

67
00:03:21.518 --> 00:03:23.735
<i>[Man] All right.
[Woman] Okay. man.</i>

68
00:03:23.804 --> 00:03:27.556
<i>Here we go.</i> Get up.
You all right? [Groans]

69
00:03:27.624 --> 00:03:30.174
Uh. did I score. man? Oh. yeah.

70
00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.394
You had a hat trick.
Come on. [Groans]

71
00:03:33.414 --> 00:03:35.697
I do not know how
I feel about this.

72
00:03:35.766 --> 00:03:37.966
- It's very primal.
- I like it...

73
00:03:38.034 --> 00:03:40.001
just a little too much.

74
00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.150
<i>[Woman] Come on. team.
[Player] Come on. Let's focus.</i>

75
00:03:44.641 --> 00:03:47.408
[Booth. Groans] So.
you still seein' double?

76
00:03:47.477 --> 00:03:50.807
- Only when I open
more than one eye.
- [Laughs]

77
00:03:50.831 --> 00:03:54.900
- Your hand's busted.
- Yeah. well. you know. Guy left his helmet on.

78
00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:59.655
- Hey. you two all right?
- <i>[Men Chuckling. Chattering]</i>

79
00:03:59.723 --> 00:04:01.857
- Wow.
- What?

80
00:04:01.925 --> 00:04:05.277
Wanna wait outside? Your hand might
be broken. You want me to look at it?

81
00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:07.440
No. it's all right. You
can wait outside. please.

82
00:04:07.464 --> 00:04:10.599
It's a men's locker
room. Bones. <i>[Man] Bye.</i>

83
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:18.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

84
00:04:22.912 --> 00:04:24.846
<i>[Man] There comes
a time in ice fishing...</i>

85
00:04:24.914 --> 00:04:28.199
when it's time for the father to
turn the drilling over to his son.

86
00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.571
[Chuckles] Man.
this is a great day.

87
00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:37.692
Hey. you give me beer. let
me run the auger. Yep. [Sighs]

88
00:04:37.761 --> 00:04:41.379
You're 18. Leo. You start
drillin' holes. it's safety first.

89
00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.749
You got me? Yeah.

90
00:04:43.817 --> 00:04:48.369
Nothin' I'm saying here applies
only to ice augers. You get me?

91
00:04:49.523 --> 00:04:51.439
Oh. [Chuckles] All right.

92
00:04:51.508 --> 00:04:55.021
Good. You know. that way you
don't fall through the ice and die...

93
00:04:55.045 --> 00:04:57.412
or get a disease
or get pregnant...

94
00:04:57.481 --> 00:04:59.331
Dad. come on. [Clears Throat]

95
00:05:01.284 --> 00:05:03.235
Go ahead. All right.

96
00:05:04.388 --> 00:05:08.423
Attaboy. Keep her perpendicular!

97
00:05:08.492 --> 00:05:10.486
[Drilling Continues]
Once you get in a little bit.

98
00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:12.488
you can speed her
up. let 'er rip. [Chuckles]

99
00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:14.446
All right. Let her rip.

100
00:05:16.499 --> 00:05:18.249
Dad. she... she's bleeding.

101
00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:22.504
- Uh. she's bleeding. Look!
- Pull out. Pull out!

102
00:05:22.573 --> 00:05:24.573
[Motor Stops]

103
00:05:25.909 --> 00:05:27.859
Oh. I hope that's a fish.

104
00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:35.466
You better go wait in the truck.

105
00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:43.091
<i>[Police Radio Chatter]</i> What
do you think there. Bones?

106
00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:47.162
I would surmise that the body went into the
lake before it froze. then the lake froze.

107
00:05:47.231 --> 00:05:50.966
<i>then the body floated up and became
attached to the bottom of the ice.</i>

108
00:05:51.034 --> 00:05:54.636
- I meant. was he murdered?
- Oh. Um. maybe.

109
00:05:54.704 --> 00:05:59.206
Could've been... an
accident or a suicide. except...

110
00:06:00.543 --> 00:06:02.978
- You shouldn't do that.
- It itches. okay?

111
00:06:03.046 --> 00:06:05.380
Yeah. well. except for what?

112
00:06:05.449 --> 00:06:09.501
Trauma to the left maxillary
orbit suggests violence.

113
00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:11.997
- It's kind of gross.
what you're doing.
- Gross?

114
00:06:12.021 --> 00:06:13.988
You got your finger in
some guy's maxillary orbit.

115
00:06:14.057 --> 00:06:16.491
I don't think there's anything
else to be learned here. so...

116
00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.560
let's get this Popsicle
back to the lab.

117
00:06:18.629 --> 00:06:22.497
- Hey. look at that. Bones made a joke.
- Well. I can be quite amusing.

118
00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:28.353
- Wait a second.
- Booth. you aren't
wearing any gloves.

119
00:06:31.859 --> 00:06:36.094
Bones. I... Remember that guy I punched
out last month during my hockey game?

120
00:06:37.247 --> 00:06:39.458
Pete Carlson? Yes.
when you broke your hand.

121
00:06:39.482 --> 00:06:41.399
That's him.

122
00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:48.590
I'm a suspect. Here.

123
00:07:29.816 --> 00:07:33.184
<i>Given that Agent Booth is currently
the prime suspect in this murder...</i>

124
00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:36.598
Uh. we don't know it's murder. Huh.
look at that. I'm the prime suspect.

125
00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:39.741
Agent Payton Perotta here
will be working with Dr. Brennan.

126
00:07:39.809 --> 00:07:42.426
I won't work the
case without Booth.

127
00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:44.640
In that case. I invite Agent
Booth's continued participation...

128
00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:47.833
<i>In the background.
as an adviser.</i>

129
00:07:47.901 --> 00:07:49.863
Agent Payton Perotta has
earned bachelor's degrees...

130
00:07:49.887 --> 00:07:52.087
in both forensic
science and criminology.

131
00:07:52.155 --> 00:07:55.907
Well. anything short of a doctorate
is virtually useless at my level.

132
00:07:55.976 --> 00:07:58.520
- [Caroline] How would you
like to proceed. darlin'?
- Well. it's pretty obvious.

133
00:07:58.544 --> 00:08:01.313
We definitely wanna interrogate
the primary suspect. right?

134
00:08:01.381 --> 00:08:02.947
[Quietly] Yep.

135
00:08:07.771 --> 00:08:09.816
Based on decomp.
I'd put time of death...

136
00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.901
at about five days
prior to freezing.

137
00:08:11.925 --> 00:08:14.008
Local cops say the lake
froze over three weeks ago.

138
00:08:14.077 --> 00:08:16.037
Aside from some dormant
<i>Anopheles</i> mosquito larvae.

139
00:08:16.079 --> 00:08:17.990
I imagine whatever the
water from the lake tells us.

140
00:08:18.014 --> 00:08:19.614
it'll be through a microscope.

141
00:08:19.683 --> 00:08:23.084
If Booth is a suspect. then I should
be too. This guy scrambled my brains.

142
00:08:23.153 --> 00:08:25.402
<i>Your alibi is that you
were seeing double...</i>

143
00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:27.605
<i>and being taken care
of by your mother.</i>

144
00:08:27.674 --> 00:08:30.942
I'll get on the fluid samples you
took from the lungs and esophagus.

145
00:08:31.011 --> 00:08:33.945
Could be the vic was drowned
somewhere else and then dumped in the lake.

146
00:08:34.014 --> 00:08:36.374
No. Drowning's not the way
Booth would kill someone.

147
00:08:37.267 --> 00:08:39.768
Not... that I actually...

148
00:08:39.836 --> 00:08:42.336
suspect Booth... at all.

149
00:08:43.957 --> 00:08:46.608
Quit staring at me.

150
00:08:51.081 --> 00:08:54.849
<i>In the course of the game. the
victim and I exchanged blows.</i>

151
00:08:54.918 --> 00:08:57.685
Who initiated the
fight? It was hockey.

152
00:08:57.754 --> 00:08:59.621
So it was spontaneous
combustion?

153
00:08:59.689 --> 00:09:01.873
The guy hit two of my players.

154
00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:03.619
The ref... he didn't catch that.

155
00:09:03.643 --> 00:09:04.993
And that made you angry.

156
00:09:05.061 --> 00:09:06.912
Not angry enough. you know.

157
00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:09.058
to chase him down after
the game and kill him.

158
00:09:09.082 --> 00:09:12.884
Where'd you go after the game? Uh.
Bones drove me and Wendell to the hospital.

159
00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:15.570
So no alibi that
night or the next?

160
00:09:15.639 --> 00:09:18.400
Bones and I are just
partners. <i>[Writing. Stops]</i>

161
00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:24.578
Okay. Now you're answering
questions I had no intention of asking.

162
00:09:24.647 --> 00:09:29.166
<i>Is it your contention that. uh. your argument
with the victim was constrained to the ice?</i>

163
00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:31.569
That is my contention. Mmm.

164
00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:33.622
'Cause I have a-a witness...

165
00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:35.624
who stated you told
Carlson. and I quote.

166
00:09:35.692 --> 00:09:37.125
"You get up off that ice...

167
00:09:37.193 --> 00:09:38.971
and we'll settle this
out in the parking lot."

168
00:09:38.995 --> 00:09:41.996
Trash-talking.

169
00:09:42.065 --> 00:09:45.866
- Let me cut to the chase here. Did you kill Pete Carlson?
- No.

170
00:09:45.935 --> 00:09:50.188
- Did you dump his body
in the lake?
- No. I did not. Agent Perotta.

171
00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.494
Do you feel that your experience
as the child of an abusive alcoholic...

172
00:09:57.563 --> 00:10:00.531
has made you more
prone to violence?

173
00:10:03.687 --> 00:10:05.687
Excuse me.

174
00:10:11.945 --> 00:10:13.461
What the hell are<i> you</i> doing?

175
00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:16.197
It's part of my job to assist
the interrogating agent.

176
00:10:16.265 --> 00:10:19.917
You know I didn't murder anyone. So what you're
doin' right now is you're just studying me.

177
00:10:19.986 --> 00:10:21.369
That's part of our agreement.

178
00:10:21.437 --> 00:10:24.333
You have a question for me.
you ask me yourself. Don't use her.

179
00:10:24.357 --> 00:10:26.006
All right. Okay. Two questions.

180
00:10:26.075 --> 00:10:29.928
One: Am I picking up some sexual
tension between you and Agent Perotta?

181
00:10:29.997 --> 00:10:32.437
How the hell do I know
what you're pickin' up?

182
00:10:32.499 --> 00:10:34.632
Okay. Uh. two:

183
00:10:34.701 --> 00:10:37.451
Underneath your
affable exterior...

184
00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:40.855
is a deep reservoir of rage.

185
00:10:40.924 --> 00:10:44.059
My question is. do you
always have that under control?

186
00:10:44.127 --> 00:10:47.306
You know if I didn't. you'd be dead
right now instead of just wincing.

187
00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:50.631
- I'm not wincing.
- Well. don't ever bring
my old man up again.

188
00:10:54.487 --> 00:10:57.188
<i>[Door Slams]</i>

189
00:10:57.257 --> 00:11:00.441
Rats! I winced. <i>[Door Opens]</i>

190
00:11:02.528 --> 00:11:03.978
<i>[Door Closes]</i>

191
00:11:05.165 --> 00:11:07.515
So... [Clears Throat]

192
00:11:07.584 --> 00:11:10.351
do<i> you</i> have any more questions?

193
00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.370
Thank you.

194
00:11:12.439 --> 00:11:14.455
<i>[Earpiece Hits Table]</i>
[Chuckles] Yeah. Uh...

195
00:11:14.524 --> 00:11:17.324
- You work out much?
- Yeah. I'm pretty consistent.

196
00:11:17.393 --> 00:11:20.261
You look like you take
excellent care of yourself.

197
00:11:23.366 --> 00:11:25.366
Okay. this is useless.

198
00:11:27.336 --> 00:11:30.704
Both patellas are fractured. As
though he'd fallen to his knees?

199
00:11:30.773 --> 00:11:32.706
Yeah. with a
great deal of force.

200
00:11:32.775 --> 00:11:35.860
- During a hockey game?
- No. Not if he wore pads.

201
00:11:35.929 --> 00:11:38.262
I believe that this is
the cause of death.

202
00:11:39.265 --> 00:11:41.683
Penetration of the
lachrymal sac here.

203
00:11:41.751 --> 00:11:44.085
deep into the
inferior orbital fissure.

204
00:11:44.154 --> 00:11:46.387
Yeah. I would've thought
a small-caliber bullet. but...

205
00:11:46.456 --> 00:11:49.056
No sign of bullet
fragments. Yeah.

206
00:11:53.629 --> 00:11:56.864
This is Pete's apartment. He
wasn't the best housekeeper.

207
00:11:56.933 --> 00:11:59.633
<i>Miss Withers. was Mr. Carlson
up-to-date on his rent?</i>

208
00:11:59.702 --> 00:12:02.536
Ah. good question. Great start.

209
00:12:02.605 --> 00:12:06.657
<i>Uh. yes. mostly...
500 bucks short.</i>

210
00:12:06.726 --> 00:12:10.311
<i>He didn't need much.
He was a big kid at heart.</i>

211
00:12:10.379 --> 00:12:12.496
Poor Pete.

212
00:12:12.565 --> 00:12:14.482
What he really loved was hockey.

213
00:12:14.551 --> 00:12:18.069
<i>I wouldn't be surprised if that's why
he joined the volunteer fire department.</i>

214
00:12:18.138 --> 00:12:22.006
I even got him this necklace.

215
00:12:22.075 --> 00:12:25.559
- Some crossed hockey sticks.
- <i>[Camera Shutter Clicks]</i>

216
00:12:25.628 --> 00:12:29.096
- You attended his games?
- Oh. all of 'em. Yeah.

217
00:12:29.165 --> 00:12:31.882
You were a couple?

218
00:12:31.951 --> 00:12:36.554
<i>It looks like someone went through all of his
belongings and then left them on the floor.</i>

219
00:12:36.623 --> 00:12:38.417
Oh. it always looked like that.

220
00:12:38.441 --> 00:12:40.741
The car outside with
the flat tires... is that his?

221
00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:44.045
Yeah. Somebody slashed the
tires just before he disappeared.

222
00:12:44.114 --> 00:12:46.125
Why didn't you
report him missing?

223
00:12:46.149 --> 00:12:48.215
I thought. maybe. mmm...

224
00:12:48.284 --> 00:12:50.751
I thought he was staying
with someone else.

225
00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:54.088
There's a lot of bills here:
"Final Notice." "Past Due."

226
00:12:54.157 --> 00:12:56.818
Looks like he couldn't
afford to feed his fish either.

227
00:12:56.842 --> 00:13:00.194
"Albie... Thursday. 11:00 p.m."

228
00:13:01.297 --> 00:13:04.365
- Do you know who Albie is?
- I don't know.

229
00:13:04.434 --> 00:13:07.885
- This is blood.
- It's a hockey jersey. Bones.

230
00:13:07.954 --> 00:13:10.237
Hockey players bleed sometimes
when they play the game.

231
00:13:10.306 --> 00:13:12.723
Miss Withers. how bad
were his financial problems?

232
00:13:12.793 --> 00:13:15.493
<i>Well. a couple days
before Pete disappeared.</i>

233
00:13:15.562 --> 00:13:18.245
he asked me for $2.000.

234
00:13:18.314 --> 00:13:20.481
Did he say what for?

235
00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:23.317
He liked me. you know?

236
00:13:23.386 --> 00:13:26.954
He was one of these guys...
He... He didn't say much.

237
00:13:27.023 --> 00:13:28.822
<i>but he could be real sweet.</i>

238
00:13:28.891 --> 00:13:30.870
And a man borrows
money from a woman...

239
00:13:30.894 --> 00:13:34.062
It means there's a
bond of trust. right?

240
00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:36.581
I don't understand
your reasoning. I do.

241
00:13:36.649 --> 00:13:39.361
It's definitely a... bond of
trust. You're absolutely right.

242
00:13:39.385 --> 00:13:42.637
We're terribly
sorry for your loss.

243
00:13:50.747 --> 00:13:52.780
Is that our victim? Yes.

244
00:13:52.849 --> 00:13:54.916
The last of the tissue samples.

245
00:13:54.984 --> 00:13:57.663
Wendell can clean the skeleton
now. and you can do your thing.

246
00:13:57.687 --> 00:14:01.989
Oh. you still think the cause of death
was a projectile through the left eye?

247
00:14:02.058 --> 00:14:05.326
Yes. but since we found
no bullet. nor any indication...

248
00:14:05.395 --> 00:14:08.762
of gunpowder residue in the wound. we're
stumped as to what kind of projectile.

249
00:14:08.831 --> 00:14:14.218
The alveolus around the incisor is
cracked. the socket caked with blood.

250
00:14:14.287 --> 00:14:17.504
- This is a recent loss.
- Well. he was a hockey player.

251
00:14:17.573 --> 00:14:21.392
- So basically we're talking
about gladiators.
- And I love it.

252
00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:23.978
Perhaps the sight
of males battling...

253
00:14:24.047 --> 00:14:26.680
stimulates the
part of your brain...

254
00:14:26.749 --> 00:14:29.195
which has so far failed
to find a suitable mate.

255
00:14:29.219 --> 00:14:31.018
And thank God you're here.

256
00:14:31.087 --> 00:14:35.056
The water I found in the victim's
esophagus... not from the lake.

257
00:14:35.124 --> 00:14:37.324
Lake water is
microorganism infested.

258
00:14:37.393 --> 00:14:39.753
Water in his throat...
Deionized brine water.

259
00:14:39.796 --> 00:14:43.147
He was killed. then dumped in
the ocean. then dumped in the lake?

260
00:14:43.215 --> 00:14:46.295
Deionized brine water freezes
clear. Contains an anti-freezing agent...

261
00:14:46.319 --> 00:14:48.781
- which I know sounds
counterintuitive...
- Ice rinks!

262
00:14:48.805 --> 00:14:50.305
<i>[Chuckles]</i>

263
00:14:50.373 --> 00:14:53.341
Kind of jumped my punch
line there. Dr. B. But yes.

264
00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:57.911
We should see what rinks are closest
to the lake. It's the one Booth played at.

265
00:14:57.980 --> 00:15:01.999
I find it interesting that the evidence
keeps pointing toward Booth.

266
00:15:19.402 --> 00:15:23.571
- <i>Pete Carlson was murdered?</i>
- Pete... he's indestructible.

267
00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:27.074
<i>Not so indestructible. This guy
took him down a few notches.</i>

268
00:15:27.143 --> 00:15:30.911
<i>Made him stay down too.</i> It was the heat
of the game. Your guy crossed the line.

269
00:15:30.980 --> 00:15:33.159
Yeah. he was our enforcer.
Took the job real serious.

270
00:15:33.183 --> 00:15:36.917
Well. whoever got Pete must've got
a drop on him. Pete wouldn't go easy.

271
00:15:36.986 --> 00:15:39.420
You mind my asking why
nobody reported him missing?

272
00:15:39.489 --> 00:15:42.251
The night after you flattened Pete.
we go up against the state police.

273
00:15:42.275 --> 00:15:44.786
Pete gets into a beef with a
big state police left-winger.

274
00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:49.380
<i>'Cause you handed him his ass on a platter.
Pete maybe had somethin' to prove that night.</i>

275
00:15:49.449 --> 00:15:51.732
- You got a name?
- Hey. Alex!

276
00:15:51.801 --> 00:15:54.802
Yo! <i>Come here.</i>

277
00:15:54.871 --> 00:15:58.539
The Fuzz player that Pete got into it with
his last game... you remember his name?

278
00:15:58.607 --> 00:16:01.837
- Yeah. Lou Herrin. Number Five.
- So Pete took Herrin down
with a real cheap shot.

279
00:16:01.861 --> 00:16:03.822
He got tossed out
the rest of the season.

280
00:16:03.846 --> 00:16:07.765
Any chance that Pete and this guy
Herrin continued their fight off the ice?

281
00:16:07.834 --> 00:16:10.162
People threaten. Yeah.
but nobody carries through.

282
00:16:10.186 --> 00:16:11.864
Yeah. Keep it on the ice. right?

283
00:16:11.888 --> 00:16:16.490
If I were you. I would talk
to Chloe. Who's Chloe?

284
00:16:16.559 --> 00:16:19.288
<i>- [Player] Chloe Bratton.
- [Player #2] Chloe's a puck bunny.</i>

285
00:16:19.312 --> 00:16:21.340
Her and Pete put in some quality
mattress time before he dumped her.

286
00:16:21.364 --> 00:16:25.132
Well. a mattress really isn't. uh.
Chloe's style. but. uh... No offense.

287
00:16:25.201 --> 00:16:27.968
None taken. Favor
backseats myself.

288
00:16:28.037 --> 00:16:29.520
[Chuckles]

289
00:16:33.826 --> 00:16:36.277
<i>I can't believe Pete's gone.</i>

290
00:16:36.346 --> 00:16:40.381
How long ago did you
two break up? Break up?

291
00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:43.045
- We didn't break up.
- His teammates
think you did.

292
00:16:43.069 --> 00:16:45.753
No. We had this
on-again. off-again thing.

293
00:16:45.822 --> 00:16:49.823
<i>It was casual. No biggie.</i> So-So you didn't
mind that he slept with different women?

294
00:16:49.892 --> 00:16:54.295
I wouldn't have minded if he
did. but I happen to know he didn't.

295
00:16:54.364 --> 00:16:57.014
Oh. I happen to
know that he did.

296
00:16:57.083 --> 00:16:58.766
- [Quietly] Right.
- Who?

297
00:16:58.835 --> 00:17:03.304
Oh. it doesn't matter. does it. given
that your relationship was so. um. casual?

298
00:17:03.373 --> 00:17:05.584
- You slashed his tires.
didn't you?
- Agent Booth.

299
00:17:05.608 --> 00:17:08.675
- No.
- We can prove you did it.
Chloe. So here's the deal.

300
00:17:08.744 --> 00:17:11.407
You tell us the truth from now
on. and we won't charge you...

301
00:17:11.431 --> 00:17:14.176
with vandalism and
obstruction of justice. okay?

302
00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:16.262
Let's try this again. You
slashed... Agent Booth.

303
00:17:16.286 --> 00:17:18.564
[Quietly] Yes. Of course.

304
00:17:18.588 --> 00:17:21.708
Let's try this again. You
slashed his tires. didn't you?

305
00:17:22.725 --> 00:17:24.825
Yes.

306
00:17:24.894 --> 00:17:27.895
I mean. he was sleeping
with someone else.

307
00:17:27.964 --> 00:17:30.698
I got passions that
take over sometimes.

308
00:17:30.767 --> 00:17:35.136
You know how it is when the guy you give
yourself to just goes off with someone else.

309
00:17:36.689 --> 00:17:39.657
- Who's. um. Albie?
- Albie?

310
00:17:41.327 --> 00:17:45.095
Albie runs this poker game in back
of a Chinese food joint off I Street.

311
00:17:45.164 --> 00:17:49.983
Probably why Pete was broke all the time.
So who'd you say Pete was sleeping with?

312
00:17:50.052 --> 00:17:52.881
I think we've got enough
information for today. Miss Bratton.

313
00:17:52.905 --> 00:17:56.323
- Thank you very much
for your cooperation.
- <i>[Booth] Thanks.</i>

314
00:17:59.144 --> 00:18:01.607
[Saroyan] Any luck with
the murder weapon? Yes.

315
00:18:01.631 --> 00:18:04.398
We are certain it
is not a screwdriver.

316
00:18:04.467 --> 00:18:07.267
Well. the blood on the
victim's jersey was all his own.

317
00:18:07.336 --> 00:18:11.405
The rib cage has
been bruised. It has?

318
00:18:11.474 --> 00:18:15.542
<i>Yes. See this vague
pattern of bone bruising?</i>

319
00:18:15.611 --> 00:18:17.639
<i>[Wendell] Yeah. it extends
from the right clavicle...</i>

320
00:18:17.663 --> 00:18:20.113
<i>through anterior ribs
four through eight.</i>

321
00:18:20.182 --> 00:18:23.116
He was... struck repeatedly.

322
00:18:23.186 --> 00:18:26.053
What. by a hockey stick?
During the game maybe?

323
00:18:26.121 --> 00:18:30.341
<i>Not during. The. um. padding
would prevent that kind of bruising.</i>

324
00:18:30.409 --> 00:18:33.794
I'll take a closer look. Uh. I
can't believe I missed that.

325
00:18:37.717 --> 00:18:40.234
[Mouths Word]

326
00:18:43.089 --> 00:18:45.989
No. I can't believe
you missed that either.

327
00:18:54.016 --> 00:18:56.283
I was signaling you to
encourage Wendell...

328
00:18:56.352 --> 00:18:58.669
by saying. "Anyone
could've missed that." but...

329
00:18:58.738 --> 00:19:00.654
You should've said so.

330
00:19:00.723 --> 00:19:02.843
Booth says I stink at
nonverbal communication.

331
00:19:05.828 --> 00:19:07.595
[Whispering] She
said in the back.

332
00:19:07.664 --> 00:19:11.382
Okay. Just don't be pullin' your
gun until you go through the kitchen.

333
00:19:11.451 --> 00:19:13.529
or mama-san there is
gonna hit the panic button.

334
00:19:13.553 --> 00:19:15.536
Got it? Okay. just go.

335
00:19:19.175 --> 00:19:21.008
[Murmurs]

336
00:19:21.077 --> 00:19:23.922
So you're ready to risk a gunfight
with your weapon in the wrong hand.

337
00:19:23.946 --> 00:19:25.657
I don't have a wrong
hand. I'm curious.

338
00:19:25.681 --> 00:19:28.727
When you shoot with your left hand. does
it feel like somebody else is shooting?

339
00:19:28.751 --> 00:19:29.751
Easy!

340
00:19:31.988 --> 00:19:33.521
Ah.

341
00:19:36.392 --> 00:19:38.992
What do we do now? Okay. F.B.I.

342
00:19:39.061 --> 00:19:42.379
<i>Okay. I'd reach for my badge
right now. but. you know. I...</i>

343
00:19:42.448 --> 00:19:45.833
- Drop your weapons. please.
- Please. The F.B.I. does not say "please."

344
00:19:45.901 --> 00:19:50.137
Okay. look. I really don't
care about the illegal gambling.

345
00:19:50.206 --> 00:19:53.991
<i>I just wanna talk to
a guy named Albie...</i>

346
00:19:54.059 --> 00:19:56.193
about a guy named Pete Carlson.

347
00:19:59.549 --> 00:20:01.549
[Guns Uncock]

348
00:20:02.552 --> 00:20:04.018
I'm Albie.

349
00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:10.908
First rule. don't kill the
people who owe you money.

350
00:20:10.976 --> 00:20:13.204
All you get then is
trouble and no money.

351
00:20:13.228 --> 00:20:16.831
How much money
did Carlson owe you?

352
00:20:16.899 --> 00:20:19.728
Okay. So. you got your operation
shut down and moved out?

353
00:20:19.752 --> 00:20:22.864
Because I could have my guys
here in about. what. three minutes...

354
00:20:22.888 --> 00:20:25.506
to mop that back room up.

355
00:20:25.574 --> 00:20:27.869
Pete Carlson was not a
bad player most of the time.

356
00:20:27.893 --> 00:20:29.871
but. you know. every
once in a while...

357
00:20:29.895 --> 00:20:31.495
He got brave and
lost everything.

358
00:20:31.547 --> 00:20:34.181
- Gamble a bit yourself. do you?
- I'm reformed.

359
00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:36.934
Tell me. when was the last
time Carlson got. um. "brave"?

360
00:20:37.002 --> 00:20:40.504
Last month. But he paid up
in full a couple of days later.

361
00:20:40.573 --> 00:20:42.623
Cash?

362
00:20:47.597 --> 00:20:49.824
A little garish.
don't you think?

363
00:20:49.848 --> 00:20:53.784
- I don't know where Pete got it.
but it covered his debt.
- I'm gonna have to take this.

364
00:20:53.852 --> 00:20:57.571
If I didn't intend to give it to
you. you'd never have seen it.

365
00:20:57.640 --> 00:21:01.726
Okay. you gave me the time I needed to
move my operation. I gave you evidence.

366
00:21:01.794 --> 00:21:03.461
<i>I call us square.</i>

367
00:21:03.529 --> 00:21:07.748
You decide to get back into
the game. you look me up.

368
00:21:07.817 --> 00:21:09.400
Right. Yeah.

369
00:21:11.103 --> 00:21:13.470
Well. we gonna call this in?

370
00:21:13.539 --> 00:21:17.241
Oh. no point. Like the
woman said. she's moved on.

371
00:21:20.312 --> 00:21:24.582
Hodgins confirmed that the traces of
rink water in the victim's esophagus...

372
00:21:24.651 --> 00:21:27.251
[Murmurs] came from this rink.

373
00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:29.898
Well. how did rink ice get
into his throat? He was beaten.

374
00:21:29.922 --> 00:21:32.200
then a sharp instrument
was thrust into his eye.

375
00:21:32.224 --> 00:21:35.375
There should be... blood stains.

376
00:21:36.629 --> 00:21:39.263
You're going to scan the
ice with one little wand?

377
00:21:39.331 --> 00:21:42.199
I'll call an F.B.I. forensics team.
We'll have the whole place searched.

378
00:21:42.268 --> 00:21:45.335
No need. All you need
is black light. right?

379
00:21:45.404 --> 00:21:48.389
Yes. Right? I got
a great idea. Just...

380
00:21:48.457 --> 00:21:51.324
Whoa. Stay here. It's
very slippery. Don't move.

381
00:21:53.395 --> 00:21:56.930
<i>[Booth] Ready? How's
that. huh? [Brennan] Nice.</i>

382
00:21:56.999 --> 00:21:59.567
[Perotta] Wow. Gonna work?

383
00:21:59.635 --> 00:22:02.286
Well. I see some.
uh. flecks of blood.

384
00:22:02.354 --> 00:22:06.607
<i>No. we're looking for something
bigger than these small specks and spots.</i>

385
00:22:06.676 --> 00:22:09.704
If the victim was stabbed in the eye. we're
looking for a pretty significant puddle.

386
00:22:09.728 --> 00:22:12.724
<i>Two guys get into a beef. then
they put their street clothes on...</i>

387
00:22:12.748 --> 00:22:15.782
and then come back here
on the ice and duke it out?

388
00:22:15.851 --> 00:22:17.868
Booth. Yeah.

389
00:22:19.271 --> 00:22:22.084
<i>[Booth] Whoa.
[Perotta] Oh. my God.</i>

390
00:22:22.108 --> 00:22:25.525
This is going to turn out to be
where Pete Carlson was murdered.

391
00:22:34.403 --> 00:22:37.238
<i>[Device Beeps]</i> This is all
the ice from the crime scene.

392
00:22:37.306 --> 00:22:39.406
including the scrapings
from the Zamboni.

393
00:22:39.475 --> 00:22:43.444
We should be able to get enough D.N.A. out
of this to confirm the blood is Carlson's.

394
00:22:43.512 --> 00:22:46.563
Whoa. Human tooth.

395
00:22:46.632 --> 00:22:49.717
It's hockey. That Zamboni
probably had a hundred teeth in there.

396
00:22:52.771 --> 00:22:55.806
Looks like we found
where the tooth fairy winters.

397
00:22:59.729 --> 00:23:02.779
[Sighs] Did you find a
match yet? <i>Just started.</i>

398
00:23:02.848 --> 00:23:04.998
Shows it's definitely
the victim's blood.

399
00:23:05.067 --> 00:23:06.879
I still haven't found
the murder weapon.

400
00:23:06.903 --> 00:23:11.389
I still haven't identified the nylon
polymer I found on the victim's shirt.

401
00:23:11.457 --> 00:23:13.690
<i>So I've looked at. like.
a thousand photos...</i>

402
00:23:13.759 --> 00:23:17.188
of those blood patterns at the
rink and tons from the apartment.

403
00:23:17.212 --> 00:23:20.314
- Why? What are you lookin' for?
- Here's a blood pattern
at the rink.

404
00:23:20.383 --> 00:23:22.382
The body was
dragged in that direction.

405
00:23:22.451 --> 00:23:25.297
Yeah. the body was dragged that
way. but what are those drops over there?

406
00:23:25.321 --> 00:23:28.021
What drops? Those
drops right there.

407
00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:31.909
<i>They parallel the dragging
body. And they aren't smeared.</i>

408
00:23:31.977 --> 00:23:34.862
These parallel drops
aren't from the victim.

409
00:23:34.931 --> 00:23:37.364
They're from whoever
dragged him across the ice.

410
00:23:37.433 --> 00:23:40.117
Well. that means we have to
check for more than just Pete's D.N.A.

411
00:23:40.185 --> 00:23:42.202
<i>Too bad we can't
question the fish.</i>

412
00:23:43.522 --> 00:23:46.607
- What killed those fish?
- Not eating for three weeks?

413
00:23:46.676 --> 00:23:48.575
If that happened. they
would eat each other.

414
00:23:48.644 --> 00:23:49.910
Oh...

415
00:23:51.747 --> 00:23:53.931
Grab your coat. We're
goin' on a field trip.

416
00:23:53.999 --> 00:23:57.935
And tell Cam to check the rink samples to find
out if there was a second source of D.N.A.

417
00:23:58.003 --> 00:24:00.163
<i>I-I'm not really
a big fan of this...</i>

418
00:24:01.106 --> 00:24:03.807
"barking out orders" stuff.

419
00:24:03.876 --> 00:24:05.876
<i>[Cell Phone Beeping]</i>

420
00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:10.340
<i>[Sweets] Agent
Booth? [Booth] Mmm?</i>

421
00:24:10.383 --> 00:24:13.600
It's come to the attention
of the deputy director...

422
00:24:13.669 --> 00:24:16.103
that you are a viable
suspect in a murder case.

423
00:24:16.172 --> 00:24:20.558
Right. Okay. and he wants you
to make sure that I'm<i> not</i> viable.

424
00:24:20.626 --> 00:24:23.071
That's correct. Come on. Sweets.
You know I didn't kill anyone.

425
00:24:23.095 --> 00:24:25.295
So. you know. put
that in shrink talk.

426
00:24:25.363 --> 00:24:28.476
and... write out your
little form and send it in.

427
00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:31.502
Mmm. Mm-hmm. Yes.
of course. But to do that.

428
00:24:31.571 --> 00:24:34.655
- I need to ask you
some questions.
- [Sighs]

429
00:24:34.723 --> 00:24:37.268
All right. [Clears
Throat] Shoot.

430
00:24:37.292 --> 00:24:41.795
I saw you in that game. You
beat another man to the ice.

431
00:24:41.864 --> 00:24:44.209
It's hockey. I was
protecting my teammate.

432
00:24:44.233 --> 00:24:48.802
- You broke your hand
on his helmet.
- It's<i> hockey.</i> okay?

433
00:24:48.871 --> 00:24:53.173
- You never played. did you?
- Oh. I've run track
and cross-country...

434
00:24:53.242 --> 00:24:56.426
and did some wrestling
and ch... <i>[Laughing]</i>

435
00:24:56.495 --> 00:24:58.095
Chess. <i>No.</i>

436
00:24:58.164 --> 00:25:00.247
- Checkers?
- Didn't say that.

437
00:25:00.315 --> 00:25:04.234
You know what? Then you know
nothing. It's about<i> teams.</i> okay?

438
00:25:04.303 --> 00:25:06.965
And<i> teamwork?</i> Obviously you don't
know anything about that. Dr. Sweets.

439
00:25:06.989 --> 00:25:09.139
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. mm-hmm.

440
00:25:09.208 --> 00:25:11.875
You joined the army.
You became a sniper.

441
00:25:11.944 --> 00:25:15.045
- Mm-hmm.
- You joined the F.B.I.

442
00:25:15.114 --> 00:25:18.581
Do you see the. uh... the
binding element in those choices?

443
00:25:20.085 --> 00:25:21.702
It's violence.

444
00:25:21.771 --> 00:25:24.504
Or the love of uniforms.
You ever think that?

445
00:25:24.573 --> 00:25:27.174
Agent Booth... <i>[Sighs]</i>

446
00:25:27.242 --> 00:25:31.561
I believe that you are
ready to confront the fact...

447
00:25:31.630 --> 00:25:33.692
that the violence you may
have suffered in childhood...

448
00:25:33.716 --> 00:25:35.877
You know what? has
followed you into adulthood.

449
00:25:35.901 --> 00:25:38.452
Fill out the form.

450
00:25:38.521 --> 00:25:41.305
<i>[Knocking]</i>

451
00:25:41.373 --> 00:25:44.024
- Not now.
- Hiya. Sweets.

452
00:25:44.092 --> 00:25:46.460
Uh. if you're about
finished here. Booth...

453
00:25:46.528 --> 00:25:48.106
<i>In accordance with the
warrant you</i> made<i> me get.</i>

454
00:25:48.130 --> 00:25:50.414
Pete Carlson's phone
records are here.

455
00:25:50.483 --> 00:25:52.710
Miss Julian. actually. I'm the one
that decides when we're done here.

456
00:25:52.734 --> 00:25:55.035
<i>Of course you are.</i>
chéri. <i>No offense intended.</i>

457
00:25:55.104 --> 00:25:57.716
I'll be deliverin' the phone
records to Agent Perotta.

458
00:25:57.740 --> 00:26:00.574
- I thought I'd do that
in your office.
- Thanks.<i> chérie.</i>

459
00:26:01.811 --> 00:26:03.310
We're done.

460
00:26:03.378 --> 00:26:06.580
Well. ye... We are done. but
that was just a coincidence.

461
00:26:06.649 --> 00:26:09.149
Sweets. I've killed. but
I've never murdered before.

462
00:26:09.217 --> 00:26:12.269
Look up the difference in your
little black book there. okay?

463
00:26:12.338 --> 00:26:14.354
<i>[Door Closes]</i>

464
00:26:15.424 --> 00:26:17.757
This is legal.
right? Absolutely.

465
00:26:17.826 --> 00:26:19.994
<i>[Wendell] Okay.</i>

466
00:26:20.062 --> 00:26:22.179
<i>[Door Closes]</i>

467
00:26:22.248 --> 00:26:24.288
None of 'em look nibbled on.

468
00:26:24.316 --> 00:26:26.278
<i>Oh. man. they should've
gone at each other...</i>

469
00:26:26.302 --> 00:26:29.436
like a Peruvian soccer
team stranded in the Andes.

470
00:26:29.505 --> 00:26:31.922
Then they all died
at the same time.

471
00:26:35.727 --> 00:26:39.079
- I don't see
what this is gonna tell us.
- How they died?

472
00:26:39.148 --> 00:26:42.148
- No. no. I... I mean. about the case.
- Ooh. hoo. hoo.

473
00:26:42.234 --> 00:26:45.352
If Brennan were here.
she'd smack your face.

474
00:26:45.421 --> 00:26:48.350
Her philosophy is. we find
out the facts about everything.

475
00:26:48.374 --> 00:26:50.307
then see how it fits together.

476
00:26:52.277 --> 00:26:55.228
Photo opportunity. Oh.

477
00:26:56.782 --> 00:27:01.435
Pete made eight calls right after
the game. but the same number.

478
00:27:01.504 --> 00:27:04.554
- Lou Herrin... who's that?
- Oh. sergeant
in the state cops.

479
00:27:04.624 --> 00:27:07.185
He exchanged blows with
the victim the night that he died.

480
00:27:07.209 --> 00:27:09.354
<i>Make it official.
Question the cop.</i>

481
00:27:09.378 --> 00:27:11.990
<i>Let's get some leverage on the guy
first... put him at the murder scene.</i>

482
00:27:12.014 --> 00:27:14.882
- Get a warrant
to test his D.N.A.
- Here we go.

483
00:27:14.950 --> 00:27:18.030
Get a warrant for this. Miss
Julian. Get a warrant for that.

484
00:27:18.054 --> 00:27:22.255
You need<i> grounds</i> for a warrant. <i>chérie.</i>
Don't they teach that at Quantico anymore?

485
00:27:22.324 --> 00:27:24.491
What grounds have
you got for that warrant?

486
00:27:24.560 --> 00:27:27.444
None. Nothin'.
You're just wishin'.

487
00:27:28.747 --> 00:27:31.598
<i>I know how to get some
blood out of this Herrin.</i>

488
00:27:31.667 --> 00:27:33.950
- Legally?
- Yeah. Of course. legally.

489
00:27:34.019 --> 00:27:37.587
- How?
- Well. there's a big game
tonight. right?

490
00:27:37.656 --> 00:27:39.923
And sometimes. durin' a game.

491
00:27:39.991 --> 00:27:41.908
people bleed. huh?

492
00:27:41.977 --> 00:27:45.261
- [Sighs] I don't like it.
- Then you don't have to show up.

493
00:27:55.007 --> 00:27:56.940
<i>[Sawing Continues]</i>

494
00:27:57.009 --> 00:27:59.276
[Exhales]

495
00:27:59.345 --> 00:28:01.945
Whoa. What are you doin'. man?
What does it look like I'm doin'?

496
00:28:02.014 --> 00:28:04.859
Think that's a good idea? You got
another couple of weeks on that cast.

497
00:28:04.883 --> 00:28:07.867
Well. considering I can't play with
a cast on. yeah. it's a great idea.

498
00:28:07.936 --> 00:28:09.286
You clear about the plan?

499
00:28:09.354 --> 00:28:11.354
If somebody bleeds.
I collect a sample.

500
00:28:11.423 --> 00:28:13.590
put it in a bag and pass
it off to Dr. Brennan.

501
00:28:13.642 --> 00:28:16.076
Lou Herrin. Number Five...
He's our prime suspect.

502
00:28:16.145 --> 00:28:18.611
And I gotta make him
bleed. <i>[Cast Cracking]</i>

503
00:28:18.680 --> 00:28:20.697
[Players Chattering]

504
00:28:20.766 --> 00:28:24.634
- <i>You've worked with Booth</i>
<i>for a while now. right?</i>
- Mm-hmm.

505
00:28:24.703 --> 00:28:29.339
Is he the kind of guy that.
uh. you know. I mean...

506
00:28:29.408 --> 00:28:33.309
Is he... flirty? Flirty?

507
00:28:33.378 --> 00:28:37.131
Would you say he twinkles
his eyes at all women?

508
00:28:37.199 --> 00:28:41.585
Twinkly eyes actually result
when the pupils dilate very wide.

509
00:28:41.653 --> 00:28:45.538
which is an unconscious result of
intense interest or sexual attraction.

510
00:28:45.607 --> 00:28:48.375
So. no. he doesn't
twinkle at everyone.

511
00:28:48.444 --> 00:28:51.344
No. All right.

512
00:28:51.413 --> 00:28:53.514
<i>[Whistle Blows]</i>

513
00:28:55.467 --> 00:28:58.836
- Is that the guy?
- That's him. Lou Herrin. Number Five.

514
00:28:58.904 --> 00:29:01.283
<i>Wow. Do you think he
even knows how to bleed?</i>

515
00:29:01.307 --> 00:29:03.489
Just keep your head up.
all right? <i>[Whistle Blows]</i>

516
00:29:07.529 --> 00:29:08.862
Ow!

517
00:29:08.931 --> 00:29:11.882
<i>[Player] Come on. You
should've called that.</i>

518
00:29:11.951 --> 00:29:14.934
<i>[Player #2] Pass
it up. That's a trip!</i>

519
00:29:25.681 --> 00:29:27.948
[Both Grunting]

520
00:29:28.017 --> 00:29:30.017
<i>[Booth] Keep your
head up. Herrin.</i>

521
00:29:34.289 --> 00:29:36.289
<i>[Brennan Shudders]</i>

522
00:29:47.703 --> 00:29:49.636
Man. what's your problem?

523
00:29:49.705 --> 00:29:53.223
I got a little chip. all right? It's Flyer
hockey. pal. This guy's hard to get mad.

524
00:29:53.292 --> 00:29:55.652
Man. he's maybe the only
one who hasn't shed a drop.

525
00:29:58.364 --> 00:30:00.280
<i>[Players Chattering]</i>

526
00:30:06.204 --> 00:30:09.122
Stay outta my crease.
Keep your head up. huh?

527
00:30:09.191 --> 00:30:11.007
[Grunts]

528
00:30:14.829 --> 00:30:17.013
- Take a warning. pal.
- [Strains]

529
00:30:17.082 --> 00:30:19.277
I think I'm finally
gettin' to this guy.

530
00:30:19.301 --> 00:30:21.250
Yeah. Hope you survive it!

531
00:30:30.746 --> 00:30:33.246
[Both Grunting]

532
00:30:46.045 --> 00:30:49.546
Ah! [Groans]

533
00:30:56.004 --> 00:30:59.205
- Taking a little break?
- [Sighs]

534
00:31:00.743 --> 00:31:04.311
- Luc Robitaille?
- Seeley Booth.

535
00:31:04.380 --> 00:31:07.497
- Right.
- Let's go. Let's play.

536
00:31:08.700 --> 00:31:10.617
Right.

537
00:31:13.472 --> 00:31:15.192
You're the greatest
left-winger of all time.

538
00:31:15.257 --> 00:31:18.491
And you're the best player on
your team. for what that's worth.

539
00:31:22.631 --> 00:31:25.991
All right. let's go. Come on.
Let's play. <i>[Stick Raps On Ice]</i>

540
00:31:29.271 --> 00:31:31.382
<i>[Robitaille] There we go.</i>

541
00:31:31.406 --> 00:31:33.723
<i>Come on. Show me something.</i>

542
00:31:33.791 --> 00:31:35.775
Head up. Attaboy.

543
00:31:37.029 --> 00:31:39.829
Come on. Move. move.
move. move. move! Let's go.

544
00:31:43.068 --> 00:31:47.003
Whoa. Wait a second. I can't play
hockey with you. I gotta solve a murder.

545
00:31:47.072 --> 00:31:49.439
You know. Booth.

546
00:31:49.508 --> 00:31:51.424
it's not about the blood.

547
00:31:51.493 --> 00:31:53.827
[Booth] It's the
best forensic clue.

548
00:31:53.895 --> 00:31:57.364
- Forget the blood.
- Then what?

549
00:31:57.433 --> 00:31:59.466
You know what makes a team.

550
00:31:59.534 --> 00:32:02.435
<i>Look at the team. It's about
what brings a team together.</i>

551
00:32:02.504 --> 00:32:05.605
The team. Look at the team.

552
00:32:05.674 --> 00:32:07.652
All right. let's go. One-on-one.
<i>[Stick Raps On Ice]</i>

553
00:32:07.676 --> 00:32:10.594
<i>Let's see what you
got. Come on. B.</i>

554
00:32:13.949 --> 00:32:18.685
Whoa! Aw. geez. I thought I
could get by you there again.

555
00:32:18.754 --> 00:32:21.204
- You'll never get by me.
- Right.

556
00:32:21.273 --> 00:32:24.224
Now listen. Booth. You're
not your father. okay?

557
00:32:24.292 --> 00:32:28.195
<i>You protect the ones you care
about on the ice and off the ice.</i>

558
00:32:28.263 --> 00:32:30.197
That's who you are.

559
00:32:30.265 --> 00:32:32.649
You're not your father. Booth.

560
00:32:32.718 --> 00:32:34.712
<i>[Echoing] You're not your
father. [Brennan] Booth?</i>

561
00:32:34.736 --> 00:32:37.337
<i>You're not your father. Booth?</i>

562
00:32:37.406 --> 00:32:38.905
Booth?

563
00:32:40.659 --> 00:32:42.759
Booth?

564
00:32:42.828 --> 00:32:45.061
Bones. what are
you doin' on the ice?

565
00:32:45.130 --> 00:32:48.715
Well. I get nervous when
you fall down and don't get up.

566
00:32:48.784 --> 00:32:51.279
Come on. Here. [Sighs]

567
00:32:51.303 --> 00:32:53.670
Up you go. buddy.
Come on. Come on.

568
00:32:59.862 --> 00:33:02.345
Don't worry. I got the blood.

569
00:33:02.414 --> 00:33:04.797
- Good work. Bones.
- But I'm Bones.

570
00:33:10.205 --> 00:33:12.439
[Whirring. Stops]

571
00:33:12.508 --> 00:33:15.492
Ugh. Smells like fish in here.

572
00:33:15.560 --> 00:33:18.111
Yeah. It's the
victim's goldfish.

573
00:33:18.180 --> 00:33:20.179
They died of ammonia poisoning.

574
00:33:20.248 --> 00:33:22.193
How did that
happen? I don't know.

575
00:33:22.217 --> 00:33:25.262
Maybe the victim washed his
aquarium with window cleaner?

576
00:33:25.286 --> 00:33:28.605
I don't know. How are
things with you and Roxy?

577
00:33:29.907 --> 00:33:32.225
Oh. good. Good.

578
00:33:32.293 --> 00:33:34.293
Taking it slow. you know.

579
00:33:34.362 --> 00:33:37.197
Letting things unfold in a...

580
00:33:37.265 --> 00:33:40.467
Are you seeing anybody? I. um...

581
00:33:40.535 --> 00:33:43.653
Actually... [Chuckles]
went out on a date last night.

582
00:33:43.722 --> 00:33:45.955
Oh. I'm glad to hear that.

583
00:33:46.024 --> 00:33:48.224
Any little twinge there?

584
00:33:48.293 --> 00:33:51.478
Definitely a little
twinge. yeah. but...

585
00:33:51.546 --> 00:33:54.130
despite the twinge. I'm glad
you're back in the saddle.

586
00:33:54.198 --> 00:33:58.401
Oh. I'm not back in the saddle
exactly. It was just a first date.

587
00:33:58.470 --> 00:34:01.321
Barely got out of
the barn. [Laughs]

588
00:34:01.390 --> 00:34:04.374
You saw the victim's
apartment. right?

589
00:34:04.442 --> 00:34:06.871
Yes. Yeah. yeah.
It was a pigsty.

590
00:34:06.895 --> 00:34:09.645
I don't think that guy
cleaned anything...

591
00:34:09.714 --> 00:34:12.815
Not with ammonia.
not with anything.

592
00:34:15.119 --> 00:34:17.504
I came as soon as I heard
Booth had a brain injury.

593
00:34:17.573 --> 00:34:20.251
What... What part of your head
hurts? The part above my shoulders.

594
00:34:20.275 --> 00:34:23.054
The doctor said he has a
concussion. He shouldn't fall asleep.

595
00:34:23.078 --> 00:34:25.144
Otherwise. not serious.

596
00:34:25.213 --> 00:34:27.541
- Tell him about
the hallucination.
- You hallucinated?

597
00:34:27.565 --> 00:34:30.516
Luc Robitaille gave me advice.

598
00:34:32.136 --> 00:34:36.272
- You got advice
on a murder case from...
- What did he say?

599
00:34:36.341 --> 00:34:39.058
He said. "Don't worry about
the... the player's blood."

600
00:34:39.127 --> 00:34:41.761
Oh. That's very interesting.

601
00:34:41.830 --> 00:34:43.896
<i>Lucky Luc told me to
look in a different direction.</i>

602
00:34:43.965 --> 00:34:46.366
[Sweets] That's interesting.
Stop saying that. Just... Stop.

603
00:34:46.435 --> 00:34:49.314
Preliminary D.N.A. tests show that
the blood mixed in with the victim's...

604
00:34:49.338 --> 00:34:51.299
did not belong to Lou Herrin.

605
00:34:51.323 --> 00:34:53.251
- Lucky Luc was right.
- <i>No. all that means...</i>

606
00:34:53.275 --> 00:34:55.436
is that you got your brains
scrambled for nothing.

607
00:34:55.460 --> 00:34:57.294
No. Lucky Luc is never wrong.

608
00:34:57.362 --> 00:35:00.425
This hallucination could be. uh.
Booth's subconscious speaking to him...

609
00:35:00.449 --> 00:35:03.689
<i>through the voice and image
of someone that he idolizes.</i>

610
00:35:03.751 --> 00:35:06.386
Like a modern version
of a vision quest?

611
00:35:06.454 --> 00:35:10.556
Oh. you know what?
Hallucination or not... [Groans]

612
00:35:10.625 --> 00:35:14.310
Lucky Luc... he told me
somethin' about myself that...

613
00:35:18.617 --> 00:35:23.119
- He told me something.
- I'd be very interested
in knowing what he said.

614
00:35:23.187 --> 00:35:25.150
Lucky for me. you're
never gonna find out...

615
00:35:25.174 --> 00:35:27.152
because Bones is
gonna drive me home...

616
00:35:27.176 --> 00:35:29.643
What? and get me soup. [Groans]

617
00:35:31.980 --> 00:35:35.898
<i>[Hodgins] There's gotta be some reason
these fish died of ammonia poisoning.</i>

618
00:35:35.968 --> 00:35:39.469
Last time I did this. I ended up
in juvie hall over the weekend.

619
00:35:39.537 --> 00:35:42.872
What? What? Uh. nothing.

620
00:35:44.309 --> 00:35:48.177
Whoa. Wow.

621
00:35:48.246 --> 00:35:50.730
Oh. wow.

622
00:35:50.799 --> 00:35:54.417
Buried treasure.
What do we do now?

623
00:35:56.004 --> 00:35:59.505
Find out why the hell he was
hiding jewelry in a fish tank.

624
00:36:02.744 --> 00:36:05.561
Have any of you ever heard of
something called "chain of evidence"?

625
00:36:05.630 --> 00:36:07.113
Miss Julian...

626
00:36:07.182 --> 00:36:09.677
Why didn't you go with these
two idiots to the victim's home?

627
00:36:09.701 --> 00:36:12.313
- Please don't call
my people idiots.
- We're not idiots.

628
00:36:12.337 --> 00:36:15.488
- I feel like an idiot.
- You don't speak right now... either of you.

629
00:36:15.557 --> 00:36:17.656
<i>[Saroyan] It's a crime scene.</i>

630
00:36:17.725 --> 00:36:20.371
My people are very often at
crime scenes. It's what we do.

631
00:36:20.395 --> 00:36:25.398
No. it's not. You've got it in your
heads that you're crime-scene types.

632
00:36:25.466 --> 00:36:29.102
This is Booth's fault for indulging your
fantasies. You are not crime-scene types.

633
00:36:29.170 --> 00:36:32.806
- <i>You are lab rats.</i>
- No chain of evidence
was broken.

634
00:36:32.874 --> 00:36:36.192
When Dr. Hodgins and Mr. Bray found
the items. they immediately called me.

635
00:36:36.261 --> 00:36:40.413
I called Booth. and when his head hurt too
much to talk to me. I called Agent Perotta.

636
00:36:40.482 --> 00:36:42.031
- Miss Julian.
- What?

637
00:36:42.100 --> 00:36:44.317
A photograph of dead
fish led them to this.

638
00:36:44.386 --> 00:36:46.486
I think that kind of
brilliance is worth it.

639
00:36:48.072 --> 00:36:50.823
You've been taken hostage
by the squints. Agent Perotta.

640
00:36:53.528 --> 00:36:57.029
Turns out these items were
reported destroyed in a fire.

641
00:36:57.098 --> 00:36:59.049
The victim was a fireman.

642
00:36:59.117 --> 00:37:01.829
The F.B.I. could check to see
if the Firedawgs put out that fire.

643
00:37:01.853 --> 00:37:04.854
Stole from the fire.
cleaned off with ammonia.

644
00:37:04.923 --> 00:37:06.901
Hidden in the
aquarium. killed the fish.

645
00:37:06.925 --> 00:37:09.759
<i>Okay. Now you</i> are<i>
straying out of your territory.</i>

646
00:37:09.827 --> 00:37:12.211
No. They got it right.

647
00:37:12.280 --> 00:37:16.766
The bracelet Agents Booth and Perotta
recovered from the victim's loan shark...

648
00:37:16.835 --> 00:37:20.186
was reported destroyed
by that same fire.

649
00:37:20.254 --> 00:37:23.940
- Hmm. My people were right.
- [Together] Your people?

650
00:37:24.009 --> 00:37:27.343
- [Together] We're Booth's people.
- Hmm.

651
00:37:31.833 --> 00:37:33.849
[Groans]

652
00:37:36.421 --> 00:37:40.072
[Sighing]

653
00:38:03.198 --> 00:38:05.131
<i>They're on the Firedawgs.</i>

654
00:38:05.200 --> 00:38:08.768
<i>but they also played on
the same high school team.</i>

655
00:38:08.837 --> 00:38:11.971
[Quietly] What brings them
together. eh? <i>[Door Opens]</i>

656
00:38:12.040 --> 00:38:14.273
I'm back.

657
00:38:14.342 --> 00:38:17.021
<i>[Door Closes]</i> [Continues Quietly]
Hey. what brings them together?

658
00:38:17.045 --> 00:38:18.978
What brings the team together?

659
00:38:19.047 --> 00:38:22.749
So I got the soup from the
place. And yes. I told "Mama"...

660
00:38:22.817 --> 00:38:26.469
that it was for you
especially. [Clears Throat]

661
00:38:26.537 --> 00:38:30.356
[Quietly] It's all about
the team there. It's all...

662
00:38:31.559 --> 00:38:33.621
What are you doing? It's
all about the team there.

663
00:38:33.645 --> 00:38:36.579
Bones. it's all about
the team there. They...

664
00:38:36.648 --> 00:38:39.649
These four guys... they all played
hockey together in high school.

665
00:38:39.718 --> 00:38:43.836
<i>and now they all play
together as a team.</i>

666
00:38:43.905 --> 00:38:48.223
They're all firemen? Yeah. they
all worked the jewelry store fire.

667
00:38:48.292 --> 00:38:51.010
One of these three
guys is the murderer.

668
00:38:51.079 --> 00:38:53.457
According to
Mr. Lucky? [Pen Clatters]

669
00:38:53.481 --> 00:38:55.431
Ow. It's Luc. okay? It is...

670
00:38:55.500 --> 00:38:59.118
<i>I-It's not "Mr. Lucky."
It is Luc Robitaille.</i>

671
00:38:59.187 --> 00:39:01.788
<i>Left wing. Great shot.</i>

672
00:39:01.857 --> 00:39:04.268
Luc Robitaille. He's one of
the best left-wingers of all time.

673
00:39:04.292 --> 00:39:07.627
- What is this?
- It's a lace puller. Why?

674
00:39:07.696 --> 00:39:10.647
I think it might be
the murder weapon.

675
00:39:12.350 --> 00:39:14.601
We want to discuss
the jewelry store fire.

676
00:39:14.669 --> 00:39:16.647
I want a lawyer. What for. Alex?

677
00:39:16.671 --> 00:39:19.689
- We didn't do anything wrong. None of us did.
- What about Pete?

678
00:39:19.757 --> 00:39:22.019
He break some kind of fireman
code. somethin' like that?

679
00:39:22.043 --> 00:39:23.837
Yeah. somethin' like that.

680
00:39:23.861 --> 00:39:26.295
I've got nothin' to say about
any of this. I want a lawyer.

681
00:39:26.364 --> 00:39:28.497
We know Carlson was
beaten with a hockey stick.

682
00:39:28.566 --> 00:39:32.851
after which. a lace puller entered his
brain through his eye and killed him.

683
00:39:32.920 --> 00:39:35.321
What about your dream. Ed?

684
00:39:35.390 --> 00:39:37.741
You were gonna
play for the NHL. right?

685
00:39:37.809 --> 00:39:42.295
<i>"Local Player Scouted by
the NHL." Look at that one.</i>

686
00:39:42.363 --> 00:39:45.882
<i>Oh. this one's good too:
"Fralic's Hat Trick Wins Game."</i>

687
00:39:47.585 --> 00:39:49.519
I got injured.

688
00:39:49.587 --> 00:39:53.673
This injury would end any chance
of a career in professional hockey.

689
00:39:53.742 --> 00:39:56.454
- What does that have to do
with anything?
- Look. I got hurt.

690
00:39:56.478 --> 00:40:00.012
Now I sell siding and play hockey on the
weekends. Why rub his face in the past?

691
00:40:00.081 --> 00:40:03.232
Who ruined you?

692
00:40:03.301 --> 00:40:05.217
Pete Carlson.

693
00:40:08.005 --> 00:40:11.590
- It was Pete.
- You all knew about
the stolen jewelry?

694
00:40:11.659 --> 00:40:13.938
Question is. how many of you
were there the night he was killed?

695
00:40:13.962 --> 00:40:17.363
None of us. Nobody here
had anything to do with that.

696
00:40:17.432 --> 00:40:21.900
We have the hockey stick.
the murder weapon and D.N.A.

697
00:40:21.969 --> 00:40:24.854
It's only a matter of time.

698
00:40:32.347 --> 00:40:34.730
Yeah.

699
00:40:34.799 --> 00:40:37.617
- What?
- It was me.

700
00:40:37.686 --> 00:40:40.564
I asked to meet Pete on
the ice after everybody left.

701
00:40:40.588 --> 00:40:43.223
I told him to give
back the stolen jewelry.

702
00:40:43.291 --> 00:40:46.392
And he said to me... He...

703
00:40:47.462 --> 00:40:51.414
He said to me that
I was a... a coward.

704
00:40:52.984 --> 00:40:54.995
that I didn't do
anything to him...

705
00:40:55.019 --> 00:40:57.487
back in the day when
he wrecked my life...

706
00:40:57.556 --> 00:40:59.676
and I wouldn't do
anything to him now.

707
00:41:03.527 --> 00:41:05.595
Well. he was wrong.

708
00:41:27.702 --> 00:41:30.681
- I'm not positive
this is a good idea.
- [Booth Chuckles]

709
00:41:30.705 --> 00:41:32.849
[Yelps] Oh. I gotcha! I
gotcha. Stay up here.

710
00:41:32.873 --> 00:41:35.085
[Laughing] Okay. It's all
right. Here we go. One more.

711
00:41:35.109 --> 00:41:37.154
You know what? I
gotta stay up all night.

712
00:41:37.178 --> 00:41:40.413
So who better to keep me
company than you? [Laughing]

713
00:41:40.481 --> 00:41:44.467
You and me skating is saving
you from slipping into a coma? Oh...

714
00:41:44.535 --> 00:41:47.336
Ah-Ah! Easy. Bones.
Now <i>I'm</i> gonna go down.

715
00:41:47.404 --> 00:41:49.689
I have a lot of
natural athletic ability.

716
00:41:49.758 --> 00:41:52.392
Oh. yeah. Natural. I can...
I can see that. [Chuckles]

717
00:41:52.460 --> 00:41:54.694
Real smooth and
natural. That's it.

718
00:41:54.763 --> 00:41:57.513
Relax. Oh. [Yelps]

719
00:41:59.400 --> 00:42:04.153
That Agent Perotta... she
really enjoyed working with us.

720
00:42:04.222 --> 00:42:06.723
Yeah. But. um.

721
00:42:08.776 --> 00:42:11.610
you're the only F.B.I.
agent I want to work with.

722
00:42:13.448 --> 00:42:18.250
- Will you tell me what the... Lucky Luciano told you?
- He's not an opera singer.

723
00:42:18.319 --> 00:42:21.153
Why do you always say that wrong?
You do it on purpose. don't you?

724
00:42:21.222 --> 00:42:23.689
I would like to
know what he said.

725
00:42:25.092 --> 00:42:28.461
He said that I'm not
like... my old man.

726
00:42:29.530 --> 00:42:31.480
He said I'm made
of better stuff.

727
00:42:31.549 --> 00:42:37.136
Well. I don't know your
"old man"... your father...

728
00:42:37.222 --> 00:42:39.922
But...

729
00:42:39.991 --> 00:42:43.592
I think you're made
of very. very good stuff.

730
00:42:44.913 --> 00:42:48.147
Hey. know what? Forget
about Agent Perotta. all right?

731
00:42:48.215 --> 00:42:50.382
Nothing's gonna change
between me and you.

732
00:42:50.451 --> 00:42:55.288
Well. entropy is a natural force that pulls
everything apart at a subatomic level.

733
00:42:55.356 --> 00:42:57.707
Everything changes.
Don't! Not everything. Bones.

734
00:42:57.775 --> 00:42:59.820
[Yelps] [Laughing]
Not everything.

735
00:42:59.844 --> 00:43:02.789
You're gonna make me fall.
I'm never gonna make you fall.

736
00:43:02.813 --> 00:43:05.910
I'm always here. You kiddin'
me? This is kinda fun actually.

737
00:43:05.934 --> 00:43:08.894
Yes. see. I can... Watch.
here comes the big spin. Uh-oh.

738
00:43:09.970 --> 00:43:13.388
[Brennan Laughs] Whoa!
[Chattering] Go easy.

739
00:43:47.141 --> 00:43:48.557
What's that mean?

739
